# Architecture rules — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

The rules every change is held to. They are enforced by the trust pipeline (see
[AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) and the testing method); this document is the
human-readable version so a reader — or the review layer — knows the standard.

## Structure as-if-portable

Every feature separates a **generic engine/method** from **project-specific
rules/config**, and app code stays free of infrastructure concerns. Apply the
same split everywhere — reusable parts keep their own dependencies and must not
import app code. This is what makes later extraction mechanical instead of a
refactor.

## Size and complexity thresholds

| Rule | Threshold | Mechanism |
|---|---|---|
| Line width | {{LINE_WIDTH}} | {{FORMATTER}} (`formatter.lineWidth`) |
| Function length | ≤ {{MAX_FUNCTION_LOC}} LOC | structure AST check |
| File length | ≤ {{MAX_FILE_LOC}} LOC | structure AST check |
| Nesting depth | ≤ {{MAX_NESTING}} | structure AST check |
| Cognitive complexity | ≤ {{MAX_COGNITIVE_COMPLEXITY}} | {{COMPLEXITY_RULE}} |
| Nested callbacks | none excessive | {{NESTED_CALLBACK_RULE}} |
| JSX inside `useMemo`/`useCallback` | forbidden ({{UI_APPS}}) | {{JSX_IN_MEMO_PLUGIN}} |
| Duplication | ≤ {{MAX_DUPLICATION}}% | {{DUPLICATION_TOOL}} (scans stage) |

Generated code ({{GENERATED_GLOBS}}), indexer config, and documentation markdown
are not code and are exempt from these checks.

## Backend layering (`{{BACKEND_DIR}}`)

```text
resolver → service → db
```

- **Resolvers** ({{RESOLVER_DIR}}) translate one field into a call. They may use
  the {{AUTH_LAYER}} helpers to authorize. A resolver **must not call another
  resolver**, and **must not touch the database** directly.
- **Services** ({{SERVICE_DIR}}) own all database access and business rules, and
  are the only layer in this path that imports {{DB_DIR}}.
- **`{{DB_DIR}}`** holds the data schema and client; it knows nothing above it.

This is architecture pattern #1 in the architecture suite ({{ARCH_TOOL}}), which
runs in the pipeline's `scans` stage.

## Frontend composition ({{UI_DIRS}})

- **{{GRAPHQL_CLIENT}} is the GraphQL client layer.** Components request data
  with it; do not hand-roll fetch calls.
- **Compose components.** Extract a new component when a piece is more than
  three things; do not grow one component into a whole page.
- **No JSX produced inside `useMemo`/`useCallback`** — those return values, not
  markup. Checked by the plugin above.
- **Reuse hooks**; a behavior that belongs in a hook lives in a hook.
- Split **server state** (query/route data) from **local or context state**; do
  not duplicate one into the other.
- Route modules stay thin and lazy-load client-only work.
